description:
POSITION SUMMARY
Under general supervision, performs daily work assignments for the Senior Center Division of the Community Services Department in accordance with the Employee Manual, Department Policies and Procedures, City of Alamogordo Ordinances, and any applicable State or Federal authority.

RECRUITMENT QUALIFICATIONS
Required:
	Associates degree in business administration, social services, or a related field;
	Three (3) years of experience in program administration;
	Two (2) years of supervisory experience;
	Valid New Mexico Drivers License with a driving record acceptable to the City of Alamogordo;
	Or any equivalent combination of education, experience, and training that provides the required knowledge, skills, and abilities.

Required within thirty (30) days of hire date:
	Complete WellSky training to access and use the on-line WellSky program; and
	Valid New Mexico Food Handler Card.

PRIMARY DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES
Essential Duties
	Manages and supervises direct-report staff by coordinating, assigning, and reviewing work to ensure compliance with policies and procedures;
	Conducts employee evaluations, introductory and annual; makes recommendations for hiring, promoting, and releasing employees; 
	Initiates and administers corrective action, as necessary, according to the Employee Manual;
	Mentors employees to full potential and ensures appropriate training is given to meet the standards of the position held;
	Maintains schedule and coordinates volunteers to assist in the daily delivery of meals under the Home Delivered Meal program;
	Delivers meals for the Home Delivered Meal program in a City vehicle, as needed;
	Gives presentations to local organizations concerning the Home Delivered Meal program;
	Conducts assessments and reassessments as required by the State of seniors unable to function independently including interviewing, completing assessment, application, and evaluation forms, compiling required information, and preparing and submitting reports, as required; maintains client records and scans records to the States AAA Data Entry Center;
	Visits, and assesses the status of senior citizens inquiring about home-delivered meals;
	Coordinates with doctors, home-care agencies, hospitals, social services, and the public by reporting senior citizens requiring assistance;
	Coordinates with local business and social organizations to assist with the procurement of home repairs for senior participants when necessary;
	Researches and develops new procedures and programs to maximize the efficiency of services provided;
	Prepares various monthly reports, including State-required assessment/reassessment reports, reports regarding volunteer hours, new projects, etc. and submits to the appropriate City/State personnel;
	Plans various programs with the Alamo Senior Center, local businesses and organizations, and Holloman Air Force Base (HAFB), including fitness days, dinner functions, and holiday programs; participates in similar events for the homebound seniors;
	Plans and coordinates food baskets and holiday gifts/meals with local businesses and organizations;
	Assists with various activities including working at dances, serving at special dinners, arranging for decorations, organizing special events, and accompanying seniors on trips;
	Assists with developing fiscal division budgets, and monitors and approves expenditures;
	Oversees inventory of supplies and completes purchase order paperwork following the Citys Procurement Code and department rules and regulations; retains files and invoices;
	Attends various meetings to address complaints and problem areas, and identify solutions;
	Greets the public in person and on the telephone, answers questions relating to Senior Center services, takes messages, and directs individuals to appropriate parties when necessary;
	Safely operates City vehicles;
	Establishes procedures to assure the highest standards of risk management, employee safety, and risk avoidance;
	Responsible for thoroughly investigating, reviewing, and addressing department or division accidents to prevent future occurrences and control risk management-related costs;
	Contributes to a high-quality work culture through participation in training and mentoring to develop skills, including safety-related training and skills;
	Interacts professionally and provides excellent customer service to all levels of City staff and citizens to ensure high operational and service standards; and
	Performs duties in accordance with the Employee Manual, Department Policies and Procedures, City of Alamogordo Ordinances, and any applicable State or Federal authority.

OTHER IMPORTANT DUTIES
	The Alamo Senior Center is a backup emergency shelter for the community, and this position may be required to train on emergency response and/or perform certain emergency services as directed; 
	Must maintain required license(s);
	Performs administrative duties, including typing correspondence, memos, and letters and filing various documents;
	Duties may be performed outside of normal business hours for special events or projects;
	Occasional travel may be necessary for training purposes;
	Maintains the confidentiality of information obtained during the performance of duties; and
	Performs such other duties as may be assigned.

The duties listed above are intended only as illustrations of the various types of work that may be performed.  The omission of specific statements of duties does not exclude them from the position if the work is similar, related, or a logical assignment to the position.

POSITION SUMMARY
Under general supervision, performs daily work assignments for the Purchasing Division of the Finance Department in accordance with the Employee Manual, Department Policies and Procedures, City of Alamogordo Ordinances, and any applicable State or Federal authority.

RECRUITMENT QUALIFICATIONS
Required:
	High School Diploma or GED equivalent;
	Two (2) years of experience in a procurement environment;
	Two (2) years of experience performing accounts payable duties;
	Obtain Certification as a NM Certified Procurement Officer within one year of hire;
	Valid New Mexico Drivers License, or the ability to obtain within sixty (60) days of employment,    with a driving record acceptable to the City of Alamogordo;
	Or, any equivalent combination of education, experience, and training which provides the  required knowledge, skills, and abilities.

Desired:
	Accounting or business classes from a higher learning institution.
	NM Certified Procurement Officer. 

PRIMARY DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES
Essential Duties
	Review purchases made with vendors to ensure compliance with threshold limits;
	Maintain purchase order filing system and register;
	Investigate and resolve purchase order problems;
	Prepare monthly department billing on various utility service charges;
	Maintain warehouse inventory and vendor liability insurance files for the City;
	Prepare and distribute documents for sealed bids, including posting bid announcements on the City website;
	Review and track bid proposals and quotes from vendors;
	Maintain bidder files, and send notice of bid awards to bid recipients and post-bid recipients   on the City website;  
	Assist in preparing reports on contract recommendations, with regard to goods and services,   for presentation to the City Commission and the general public;
	Execute and track non-taxable transaction certificates within guidelines set by the NM Tax      Law;
	Assist in maintaining the computerized procurement system by updating vendor and other      information as necessary;
	Responsible for oversite of and execution of all City auctions, including tracking and transfer  of auctioned items;
	Accurately prepare, distribute, and maintain files for annual 1099 forms;
	Provides procurement and accounts payable training to city staff;
	Provides recommendations on procurement and accounts payable policies and procedures;
	Performs complex clerical and accounts payable functions to maintain and monitor financial    record processes; 
	Prepares and tracks invoices for payment and matches to purchase orders; enters and verifies  payable documents and purchase order data in computer;
	Compiles data and prepares various reports to generate checks, including expenditure              appropriation lists (EAL), vendor lists, appropriations/expenditure reports, and quarterly          reports;
	Responsible for all city utility accounts (electric, gas, water, phone, etc.) by preparing and submitting monthly check requests with the correct documentation and ensuring the          appropriate line items are charged; 
	Reconciling vendor statements;
	Prepares and verifies vouchers and associated reports for non-purchase order payments such   as check requests, and travel;
	Answer questions and respond to complaints from the public, City departments, and vendors  with regard to procurement activities;
	Ensure office copy machine maintenance and inventory necessary for operation;
	Contribute to a high-quality work culture through participation in training and mentoring to  develop skills, including safety-related training and skills; 
	Interacts professionally and provides excellent customer service to all levels of City staff     and citizens to ensure high operational and service standards; and
	Perform duties according to City of Alamogordo Ordinances, Citywide and Departmental    Policies and Procedures, and any applicable laws regulated by an outside authority.

OTHER IMPORTANT DUTIES
	Must maintain required licenses(s) and/or certification(s);
	Assist with warehousing, distribution, and shipping as needed;
	Work outside of the normal work schedule may be required, including evenings, weekends,   and holidays;
	Maintain the confidentiality of information obtained during the performance of duties;
	On-call once per month or as rotation requires; and
	Performs such other duties as may be assigned.

The duties listed above are intended only as illustrations of the various types of work that may be performed.  The omission of specific statements of duties does not exclude them from the position if the work is similar, related or a logical assignment to the position.

POSITION SUMMARY
Under general supervision, performs daily work assignments for the Recreation Center Division of the Parks and Recreation Department. Department in accordance with the Employee Manual, Department Policies and Procedures, City of Alamogordo Ordinances, and any applicable State or Federal authority.

RECRUITMENT QUALIFICATIONS
Required:
	Must be at least 18 years of age;
	High School diploma or GED;
	One (1) year of experience in a high-volume customer service environment;
	One (1) year of cashiering experience;
	Valid CPR and First Aid certificates or the ability to obtain them within 30 days of hire;
	Valid New Mexico Drivers License or the ability to obtain within sixty (60) days of employment, with a driving record acceptable to the City of Alamogordo;
	Or any equivalent combination of education, experience, and training that provides the required knowledge, skills, and abilities.

Desired: 
	Experience working with children.

PRIMARY DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES
Essential Duties
	Assists in daily operations of the Recreation Center front desk control center, pool, and youth programs;
	Assist in overseeing operations, including front desk management, program/service provision, and facilities usage by patrons;
	Promptly and effectively interacts with patrons in person, by phone, and /or electronically, to all inquiries regarding the facilities, programs, services, and amenities provided or overseen by the Recreation Center as part of the Parks and Recreation Department;
	Perform front desk administrative duties such as facilitating and processing patron registrations, passes, permits, rentals, refunds/credits, and sponsorship applications;
	Manage patron check-in/out procedures, for example, preparing pass cards, supervising sign-in forms, collecting fees, and issuing equipment;
	Operate a multi-line phone, including answering, redirecting, and taking messages as needed.  Collect and organize any associated paperwork;  
	Maintain and balance a daily cash drawer;
	Assist in facility maintenance, including monitoring all Recreation Center areas, enforcing all facility rules and policies, inspecting all areas, and promptly reporting any issues to the appropriate higher-level staff.  Aid in maintaining facility cleanliness and performing general custodial duties;
	Provide operational support, as assigned, for events, programs, and services such as equipment set up/take down, patron transportation, sports/game scorekeeping, temporary youth participant supervision, decorating, and organizing supplies;
	Maintain up-to-date information and postings on facility marquee sign and bulletin boards;
	May fill in/substitute for co-workers, if assigned during temporary absences, by performing delegated duties sufficient to maintain normal operations;
	Provide first aid or CPR, when certified, as needed;
	Contributes to a high-quality work culture through participation in training and mentoring to develop skills, including safety-related training and skills;
	Interact professionally and provide excellent customer service to all levels of City staff and citizens to ensure high operational and service standards; and
	Perform duties in accordance with the Employee Manual, Department Policies and Procedures, City of Alamogordo Ordinances, and any applicable State or Federal authority.

OTHER IMPORTANT DUTIES
	Must obtain and maintain required license(s);
	Will work irregular hours, including shift work, nights, weekends, holidays, split shifts, and overtime hours; 
	Maintain the confidentiality of information obtained during the performance of duties; and
	Perform such other duties as may be assigned.

The duties listed above are intended only as illustrations of the various types of work that may be performed.  The omission of specific statements of duties does not exclude them from the position if the work is similar, related, or a logical assignment to the position.

POSITION SUMMARY
Under general supervision, performs daily work assignments for the Mobile Crisis Response Team (MCRT) Division of the Alamogordo Police Department, in accordance with the Employee Manual, Department Policies and Procedures, City of Alamogordo Ordinances, and any applicable State or Federal authority.  

RECRUITMENT QUALIFICATIONS
Required:
	High school diploma or GED equivalent;
	Certified Peer Recovery Specialist (CPSW) or Certified Family Support Worker (CFPSW)* in New Mexico or the ability to be certified at the next testing opportunity;
	Lived experience of recovery from a mental health condition and/or a substance use disorder;
	Valid New Mexico Drivers License, or the ability to obtain within 60 days, with a driving record acceptable to the City of Alamogordo; 
	Or any equivalent combination of education, experience, and training that provides the required knowledge, skills, and abilities.

Desired: 
	Experience with case management.

*The New Mexico Credentialing Board and Office of Peer Recovery and Engagement (OPRE) determine minimum qualifications for certifications. Testing eligibility and renewal requirements are subject to change pursuant to the Program.

PRIMARY DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES
Essential Duties
	The CIT Peer Recovery Specialist functions as an advocate, mentor, and guide to cultivate an environment characterized by mutual respect; in contrast to traditional roles, this position leverages personal experience with mental health challenges, substance use recovery, and the navigation of complex systems such as healthcare, housing, or justice systems to support peers on their path toward wellness and independence; 
	Works as a part of a mobile crisis team serving people in crisis in Otero County; 
	Assists in performing a danger assessment, a crisis assessment, an environmental assessment, and a lethality assessment upon entry to the community situation;
	Assists in performing an on-scene assessment and treatment plan;
	Performs crisis intervention, including de-escalation, crisis planning, and implementation;
	Designs appropriate referral recommendations using available community resources and follow-up;
	Maintains all incident documentation pertaining to the MCRT department;
	Serves as the on-site resource for any relevant clinical information and will be the liaison for collaboration with other involved parties, including families, friends, and other community providers (all under the clinical supervision of an independently licensed clinician);
	Provides case management duties to reduce future crisis response needs;
	Promotes self-care, illness self-management, and wellness and recovery;
	Addresses population of child, adolescent, adult, dual diagnosis, co-occurring, and elderly; 
	Works with families and involved persons to de-escalate the situation, make a crisis plan, and enlist cooperation with recommended treatment; and documents interactions;
	Provides education in the community about the agency and all components of CRS when needed;
	Safely operates a City vehicle;
	Provides mentoring to interns and new staff;
	Contributes to a high-quality work culture through participation in training and mentoring to develop skills, including safety-related training and skills;
	Interacts professionally and provides excellent customer service to all levels of City staff and citizens to ensure high operational and service standards; and
	Performs duties in accordance with the Employee Manual, Department Policies and Procedures, City of Alamogordo Ordinances, and any applicable State or Federal authority.

OTHER IMPORTANT DUTIES
	Must obtain and maintain required license(s) and/or certification(s);
	Must be able to work as a team with first responders; 
	May be required to work outside of normal business hours, including evenings, weekends, and holidays; 
	Maintains the confidentiality of information obtained during the performance of duties; and
	Performs such other duties as may be assigned.

The duties listed above are intended only as illustrations of the various types of work that may be performed.  The omission of specific statements of duties does not exclude them from the position if the work is similar, related, or a logical assignment to the position.

POSITION SUMMARY
Under general supervision, performs daily work assignments for the Administrative Division of the Parks & Recreation Department in accordance with the Employee Manual, Department Policies and Procedures, City of Alamogordo Ordinances, and any applicable State or Federal authority.

RECRUITMENT QUALIFICATIONS
Required:
	High School diploma or GED;
	Five (5) years of experience performing administrative duties in an office environment;
	Type accurately at a speed of at least 35 words per minute (verified by testing);
	Drivers License, or the ability to obtain within sixty (60) days of employment, with a driving record acceptable to the City of Alamogordo;
	Or any equivalent combination of education, experience, and training that provides the required knowledge, skills, and abilities.

Desired:
	Associates degree in business, accounting, finance, or a related field.

PRIMARY DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES
Essential Duties
	Assists the Parks & Recreation Director by performing administrative and clerical duties, including answering the phone, typing, composing letters and memorandums, preparing various types of reports, correspondence, forms, and statistical analyses, copying, filing, and distributing written materials, and handling both incoming and outgoing mail;
	Maintains the calendar of the Parks & Recreation Director by planning and scheduling meetings, conferences, teleconferences, personal appearances and/or speaking engagements, and travel;
	Greets the public in person and on the telephone, provides general information, answers questions, and directs individuals to appropriate parties, as necessary, for the Parks & Recreation Department;
	Serves as the payroll timekeeping operator for the department by entering payroll information into the timekeeping system in a timely manner; prepares and receives authorization for any payroll discrepancies for all department employees;
	Maintains the records of the Director and the department;
	Maintains, files, and enters into computer, various reports and performs record retention and destruction in accordance with State guidelines;
	Responsible for reviewing, distributing, and following up on internet emails from the public to the departments main website email address;
	Ensures that the departments information contained on the Citys website is current and accurate and reports any changes and/or discrepancies to the Citys webmaster;
	With appropriate access, may participate in making changes to the Departments website information if directed and trained by the webmaster;
	Provides clerical support for various Advisory Boards, such as Parks & Recreation and Cemetery;
	Processes and administers contracts that are recommended by Advisory Boards and approved by the Parks & Recreation Director;
	Creates meeting agendas, records minutes of meetings, and maintains files and contracts for the Advisory Boards;
	Works actively with the Advisory Boards and the Parks & Recreation Director on fiscal year budgets and strategic plans;
	Creates and compiles the Parks & Recreation brochure;
	Compiles statistical data for monthly and quarterly reports or as needed;
	Prepares monthly and quarterly financial reports required by City, State, or Federal agencies;
	Responsible for processing requisitions and approving purchase orders for supplies and equipment needed for the department and/or divisions, adhering to the purchasing guidelines;
	Receives, reviews, approves, and submits invoices to the Accounts Payable Department for payment;
	Prepares, reviews, and submits invoices to the Accounts Receivable system for collection of payments and maintains and receives records of department collections;
	Audits petty cash transactions for the divisions; completes paperwork for the reimbursement as required by City policy;
	Processes all refunds, credit, and hand check requests including vendor invoices for payment, with appropriate backup documents;
	May assist with entering and preparing the budget for all divisions within the department, coordinating with the Director and division managers;
	Reviews division budgets monthly and quarterly prepares necessary budget revisions, and notifies the Director of discrepancies;
	Processes Travel Authorization Forms for the department; completes the preliminary paperwork prior to the employees travel and posts paperwork within five working days after the employee returns;
	Processes, reports, and reconciles Federal and State grants;
	Maintains the inventory of all fixed assets, controllable property, and equipment, and tracks disposal of unserviceable property according to City ordinance;
	Maintains up-to-date knowledge of related current and pending local, State and Federal ordinances, and communicates with the Parks & Recreation Director regarding this information;
	Assists in maintaining departmental operations manual and other policies and procedures;
	Prepares personnel-related documents for division managers and assures the timely submission for approval;
	Assists with other Parks & Recreation programs, as directed or requested by the Director;
	Assists with providing information and documents in response to IPRA requests;
	Responsible for the archival of department records according to the New Mexico Municipal Records Retention Schedule;
	Attends training for professional development;
	Recommends new approaches to effect continual improvements in the efficiency of the department and services performed;
	Safely operates a City vehicle;
	Contributes to a high-quality work culture through participation in training and mentoring to develop skills, including safety-related training and skills;
	Interacts professionally and provides excellent customer service to all levels of City staff and citizens to ensure high operational and service standards; and
	Performs duties in accordance with the Employee Manual, Department Policies and Procedures, City of Alamogordo Ordinances, and any applicable State or Federal authority.

OTHER IMPORTANT DUTIES
	Must obtain and maintain required license(s);
	Duties may be performed outside of normal business hours for special events or projects;
	Occasional travel may be necessary for training purposes;
	Maintains the confidentiality of information obtained during the performance of duties; and
	Performs such other duties as may be assigned.

The duties listed above are intended only as illustrations of the various types of work that may be performed.  The omission of specific statements of duties does not exclude them from the position if the work is similar, related, or a logical assignment to the position.

RECEPTIONIST-SENIOR CENTER
(Full-Time Regular)

POSITION SUMMARY
Under general supervision, performs daily work assignments for the Senior Center Division of the Community Services Department in accordance with the Employee Manual, Department Policies and Procedures, City of Alamogordo Ordinances, and any applicable State or Federal authority.

RECRUITMENT QUALIFICATIONS
Required:
	High school graduation or its equivalent;
	One (1) year of customer service experience;
	One (1) year of cash handling experience;
	Valid New Mexico Drivers License, or the ability to obtain within sixty (60) days of employment, with a driving record acceptable to the City of Alamogordo; or 
	Any equivalent combination of education, experience, and training which provides the required knowledge, skills, and abilities.

Desired: 
	Bilingual (Spanish).
	One (1) year of clerical experience.

PRIMARY DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES
Essential Duties
	Demonstrates excellent customer service and multi-tasking skills while performing essential and other assigned duties;
	Greet the public in person and on the telephone, answers questions regarding Senior Center services and operations, take messages, and/or direct individuals to the appropriate personnel;
	Will conduct assessment and re-assessment registrations for new and existing participants following HIPAA privacy rules;
	Maintains various logs to track registration, including grocery shopping, distant van trips, classes given, etc.;
	Responsible for various monthly reports, including but not limited to monthly activity and kitchen reports;
	Assist with planning, organizing, and executing Senior Center activities and events from concept to completion, ensuring they operate smoothly and efficiently; 
	Will be required to work outside of normal business hours for scheduled activities and events sponsored by the Senior Center;
	Receives money from consumers and guests for various events and ensures proper handling and retention of money;
	Dispatches buses to senior participants homes and event locations and monitors and responds to bus radio traffic; 
	Serves as a backup driver in non-commercial City vehicles, if necessary and safely operates a City vehicle;
	Provides backup to the Senior Center Information/Resource Coordinator position;
	Contributes to a high-quality work culture through participation in training and mentoring to develop skills, including safety-related training and skills;
	Interacts professionally and provides excellent customer service to all levels of City staff and citizens to ensure high operational and service standards; and
	Performs duties in accordance with the Employee Manual, Department Policies and Procedures, City of Alamogordo Ordinances, and any applicable State or Federal authority.

OTHER IMPORTANT DUTIES
	Operate a City vehicle and serve as a backup driver as necessary;
	Provides backup to the Senior Center Information/Resource Coordinator position;
	Duties will require work being performed outside of normal working hours;
	Maintains the confidentiality of information obtained during the performance of duties; and
	Performs such other duties as may be assigned.

The duties listed above are intended only as illustrations of the various types of work that may be performed.  The omission of specific statements of duties does not exclude them from the position if the work is similar, related or a logical assignment to the position.

POSITION SUMMARY
Under general supervision, performs daily work assignments for the Street Maintenance Division of the Public Works Department, in accordance with the Employee Manual, Department Policies and Procedures, City of Alamogordo Ordinances, and any applicable State or Federal authority.

ADVANCEMENT OPPORTUNITIES
With a supervisory endorsement, and Department Director approval, a Street Maintenance Laborer II who meets the required qualifications of a Street Maintenance Worker is eligible for automatic promotion to Street Maintenance Worker pursuant to the City of Alamogordos Public Works Succession Plan.

RECRUITMENT QUALIFICATIONS
Required:
	High School Diploma or GED equivalent;
	Experience working in a construction and/or maintenance environment;
	Valid New Mexico Drivers License with a driving record acceptable to the City of Alamogordo (valid out-of-state license may be considered acceptable until NM CDL is obtained); 
	Or any equivalent combination of education, experience, and training which provide the required knowledge, skills, and abilities.

Required within six (6) months of hire date:
	Valid New Mexico Class A Commercial Drivers License with (N) endorsement and a driving record acceptable to the City of Alamogordo; and
	OSHA-compliant Flagger certification.

Desired:
	Concrete and/or asphalt experience; and
	Experience with street maintenance, signage, and striping.

PRIMARY DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES
Essential Duties
	Performs duties safely by following industry standards and properly using personal protective equipment (PPE);
	Performs various tasks related to paving, concrete, street signs, street sweeping, and alley maintenance, as assigned, including but not limited to clearing debris from work areas, shoveling, grading, sweeping, patching, painting, and weed eating;
	Safely uses and operates various construction and maintenance equipment and tools such as service trucks and water trucks, light equipment, cutting and breaking equipment, jack hammer, tamper, weed eater, pothole patcher, sand blaster, and a full range of hand and power tools;
	With use of proper tools, assists in excavation and the removal and disposal of asphalt, road base, sidewalks, curbs, driveways, alley aprons, and collars to complete assigned projects;
	Correctly and safely assists in the loading, unloading, securing, and transporting various types of equipment and supplies to and from work sites;
	Assists in traffic control on work sites, as assigned;
	Performs general equipment maintenance by routinely checking oil, water, fuel, tires, and hydraulic system on vehicles and equipment and make appropriate adjustments to ensure vehicles are in proper and safe operating condition;
	Ensures work areas and vehicles are organized and clean;
	Contributes to a safe and high-quality work culture through participation in training and mentoring to develop skills, including safety related training and skills;
	Interacts professionally and provides excellent customer service to all levels of City staff and citizens, to ensure high operational and service standards; and
	Performs duties in accordance with the Employee Manual, Department Policies and Procedures, City of Alamogordo Ordinances, and any applicable State or Federal authority.
Paving
	Assists with maintenance and repairs of roads, including hand grading, filling of holes, and cleaning of dips and ditches;
	Assists in road base preparation and sub-grading tasks related to paving;
	Obtains and distributes asphalt, seal coat, and oil to prepared road bases;
	Assists in patch sealing, including pothole repair, reconstruction of road shoulders, and crack sealing;
	Assists in patching potholes by removing loose material, filling with base material and premix, and tamping asphalt;
	Assist with asphalt paving/patching, including transporting, dumping, spreading, raking, and rolling;
	Digs out driveways, sidewalks, curbs, and asphalt; and
	Performs simple tasks associated with bridge construction and repair.
Concrete
	Assists with construction, repair, and maintenance of driveways, sidewalks, and curbs;
	Assists with concrete work, including setting forms, mixing, pouring, and finishing;
	Digs out driveways, sidewalks, and curbs; and
	Performs tasks associated with bridge construction and repair.
Streets
	Installs, repairs and replaces street signs in accordance with M.U.T.C.D. standards; 
	Paints street and parking lot lines;
	Installs street marking tapes and reflectors; and
	Maintains cleanliness of streets and gutters using street sweeping equipment.
Alleys
	Performs maintenance of City alleyways including grading, filling of holes, and cleaning of dips and ditches.

OTHER IMPORTANT DUTIES
	Must obtain and maintain required license(s) and/or certification(s);
	Upon completion of initial probationary period, required to perform on-call rotation duties outside of normal work hours including evenings, weekends, and holidays;
	Occasional non-traditional work hours may be necessary during evenings, weekends, and on holidays for emergency calls;
	Maintains the confidentiality of information obtained during performance of duties; and
	Performs such other duties as may be assigned.

The duties listed above are intended only as illustrations of the various types of work that may be performed.  The omission of specific statements of duties does not exclude them from the position if the work is similar, related or a logical assignment to the position.

POSITION SUMMARY
Under general supervision, performs daily work assignments for the Street Maintenance Division of the Public Works Department, in accordance with the Employee Manual, Department Policies and Procedures, City of Alamogordo Ordinances, and any applicable State or Federal authority.

ADVANCEMENT OPPORTUNITIES
With supervisory endorsement, and Department Director approval, a Street Maintenance Technician who meets the required qualifications of a Street Maintenance Journeyman is eligible for automatic promotion to Street Maintenance Journeyman pursuant to the City of Alamogordos Public Works Succession Plan.

RECRUITMENT QUALIFICATIONS
Required at the time of hire:
	High School Diploma or GED equivalent;
	Two (2) years of industry experience in concrete/asphalt work or street maintenance, signage, striping;
	Traffic Control Technician (TCT) certification;
	Valid New Mexico Class A Commercial Drivers License with a minimum endorsement of (N) and a driving record acceptable to the City of Alamogordo;
	Or any equivalent combination of education, experience, and training which provide the required knowledge, skills, and abilities.

Required within twenty-four (24) months of assuming a Street Maintenance Technician position:
	Traffic Control Supervisor (TCS) certification; and
	Successful completion of NM811 Excavation Law Class.

Desired:
	Pavement Marking Technician (PMT) certification

PRIMARY DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES
Essential Duties
	Responsible for proper traffic control compliance using the Manual of Uniform Traffic Control Devices (M.U.T.C.D.) standards that ensures employee safety with equal considerations for public safety and convenience;
	Performs duties safely by following industry safety standards for, and PPE including hearing and eye protection;
	With use of proper tools and equipment, excavates and removes, hauls, and disposes of asphalt, road base, sidewalks, curbs, driveways, alley aprons, and collars to complete assigned projects;
	Safely excavates, backfills, and tamps holes and trenches to grade using hand and power tools, and heavy equipment;
	Correctly and safely loads and unloads, ties down, and transports various types of equipment and supplies to and from work sites;
	Uses and operates various construction and maintenance equipment and tools such as trucks, light and heavy equipment, cutting and breaking equipment, jack hammer, tamper, and a full range of hand and power tools;
	Performs general equipment maintenance by routinely checking oil, water, fuel, tires, and hydraulic system on vehicles and equipment and makes appropriate adjustments to ensure vehicles are in proper and safe operating condition;
	Operates various equipment including but not limited to roller (rubber tire, steel wheel), backhoe, loader, forklift, motor graders, bulldozer, rotary broom, dump truck, water truck,  pickup truck,  pothole patcher, oil and asphalt distributors, paving machine, curb cutter, bobcat, street sweeper, and sand blasting unit;
	Loads materials onto trucks using front-end loaders;
	Ensures work areas and vehicles are organized and clean;
	Contributes to a safe and high-quality work culture through participation in training and mentoring to develop skills, including safety related training and skills;
	Interacts professionally and provides excellent customer service to all levels of City staff and citizens, to ensure high operational and service standards; and
	Performs duties in accordance with the Employee Manual, Department Policies and Procedures, City of Alamogordo Ordinances, and any applicable State or Federal authority.
Paving
